[7] VERDICT
========================================================================================================
  C1 = +6.56e-17 (vs -2: NO)   C2 = +6.96e-17 (vs 2: NO, degenerate)   C3 = +3.90e-16 (vs 0: YES)
  (a) FIRES: d ln(sigma/Lambda_MS^2)/d ln a = 0  =>  sigma proportional to Lambda^2,
      sigma/Lambda_MS^2 = 3.3991 = O(1)  =>  consistent with mu6, mu-4's sigma_B/sigma_C is wrong.
  (b) does NOT fire: d ln sigma/d ln a = 0, not -2  =>  sigma proportional to 1/a^2 is EXCLUDED
      as a statement about the physical tension, and mu-4's coefficient 2g^2N is falsified by
      21.9x drift.
  (c) NOT invoked as 'no pure power': the beta-dependence IS a pure power -- but of a*Lambda_MS
      (exponent exactly 2.000000), NOT of x. mu6 got the right scale and the wrong variable:
      x/(a Lambda) drifts 1.52x across the window and the local exponent is not constant
      (3.50 -> 2.28), so 2.63 is an average, not a law.
  CAVEAT [T]: with a^-1 taken from the same Tab.13 column, C1 and C3 are identities, so the data
      certify only the O(1) number sqrt(sigma)/Lambda_MS = 1.8437 -- not an independent exponent.
